    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Logistic Regression: Probability, Odds & Classification\"\ndescription: \"Understand logistic regression as a probabilistic classifier and connect log-odds, thresholds, calibration and classification metrics.\"\nauthor: \"MLStation\"\ndate: 2026-10-01\ncategories: [Statistics, Regression, Classification, Machine Learning]\ndraft: false\n---\n\n\nLinear regression predicts on the whole real line.\n\nBut a probability must stay between 0 and 1.\n\nLogistic regression solves this by modeling **log-odds**.\n\n::: {.callout-tip}\n## What you will learn\n- Probability, odds and log-odds\n- The logistic function\n- Coefficient interpretation\n- Thresholds and confusion matrices\n- Calibration versus discrimination\n:::\n\n## From a line to a probability\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{logit}(p)\n=\n\\log\\frac{p}{1-p}\n=\n\\beta_0+\\beta_1x.\n$$\n\nSolving for $p$:\n\n$$\np(x)=\\frac{1}{1+\\exp[-(\\beta_0+\\beta_1x)]}.\n$$\n\n## Interactive sigmoid\n\n```{ojs}\n//| echo: false\nviewof aLog = Inputs.range([-6,6], {value:-1, step:.1, label:\"Intercept β₀\"})\nviewof bLog = Inputs.range([-4,4], {value:1.5, step:.1, label:\"Slope β₁\"})\nsig=z=>1/(1+Math.exp(-z))\nsigcurve=d3.range(-5,5.01,.05).map(x=>({x,p:sig(aLog+bLog*x)}))\nPlot.plot({\n height:330,x:{label:\"x\"},y:{domain:[0,1],label:\"P(Y=1 | x)\"},\n marks:[Plot.line(sigcurve,{x:\"x\",y:\"p\",stroke:\"#4F46E5\",strokeWidth:3}),Plot.ruleY([.5],{strokeDasharray:\"4,4\"})]\n})\n```\n\n## Thresholds create decisions\n\nA model may output:\n\n```text\nP(fraud)=0.73\n```\n\nA business rule converts probability into action:\n\n```text\nif p ≥ threshold → flag\nelse             → do not flag\n```\n\nChanging the threshold changes false positives and false negatives.\n\n## Animation: threshold sweeps the confusion matrix\n\n::: {#861b09bd .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code code-fold=\"true\"}\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nimport plotly.express as px\n\nrng=np.random.default_rng(14)\nn=1200\nx=rng.normal(size=n)\np=1/(1+np.exp(-(-.5+1.5*x)))\ny=rng.binomial(1,p)\nrows=[]\nfor t in np.linspace(.05,.95,19):\n    pred=(p>=t)\n    tp=((pred==1)&(y==1)).sum(); fp=((pred==1)&(y==0)).sum()\n    fn=((pred==0)&(y==1)).sum(); tn=((pred==0)&(y==0)).sum()\n    for label,val in {\"TP\":tp,\"FP\":fp,\"FN\":fn,\"TN\":tn}.items():\n        rows.append({\"threshold\":round(t,2),\"cell\":label,\"count\":val})\ndf=pd.DataFrame(rows)\nfig=px.bar(df,x=\"cell\",y=\"count\",animation_frame=\"threshold\",\n           range_y=[0,n])\nfig.update_layout(height=380)\nfig.show()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:380px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"935ee6fa-dd34-4a7b-9ec0-af0121037569\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"935ee6fa-dd34-4a7b-9ec0-af0121037569\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"935ee6fa-dd34-4a7b-9ec0-af0121037569\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"threshold=0.05\\u003cbr\\u003ecell=%{x}\\u003cbr\\u003ecount=%{y}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"legendgroup\":\"\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#636efa\",\"pattern\":{\"shape\":\"\"}},\"name\":\"\",\"orientation\":\"v\",\"showlegend\":false,\"textposition\":\"auto\",\"x\":[\"TP\",\"FP\",\"FN\",\"TN\"],\"xaxis\":\"x\",\"y\":{\"dtyp